WEBVTT

NOTE Scene 02B. Speaker labels and dialogue derive from the original script.
NOTE Time positions aligned using faster-whisper word timestamps; human review still required.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
<v Jack Marlowe>The Crooked Canary was a nightclub with three kinds of customers.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.560
<v Jack Marlowe>Men who owed money, men who collected money, and men who were about to learn the

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:15.120
<v Jack Marlowe>difference. Knuckles Malone was in a corner booth, doing serious damage to a sandwich.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.220
<v Knuckles Malone>Well, well! Look what crawled outta the sewer.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.100
<v Jack Marlowe>Good evening, Knuckles.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:21.780
<v Knuckles Malone>I'm eatin', detective.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.120
<v Jack Marlowe>I can see that. What's the sandwich ever do to you?

00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:27.360
<v Knuckles Malone>Whaddaya want?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:28.440
<v Jack Marlowe>A hat.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.600
<v Knuckles Malone>There's a hat shop down the street, wise guy.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.580
<v Jack Marlowe>Ernest Cross's hat.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.400
<v Knuckles Malone>Never heard of it. Him. Whatever.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.580
<v Jack Marlowe>I didn't say what kind of hat it was.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.080
<v Jack Marlowe>You look nervous.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.640
<v Knuckles Malone>I'm not nervous. That's mustard.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.520
<v Jack Marlowe>You're sweating mustard?

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.364
<v Knuckles Malone>You got a death wish or somethin'?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.760
<v Jack Marlowe>Relax. The hat's been recovered. I'm just wondering why anybody would pay you

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.440
<v Jack Marlowe>to steal it.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.940
<v Knuckles Malone>Steal it? I was supposed to buy it! The boss only gave me fifty bucks!

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.160
<v Jack Marlowe>Sterling's getting cheap in his old age.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.080
<v Knuckles Malone>I'll say! He makes me pay for my own cab fare.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.480
<v Knuckles Malone>Wait. How'd you know it was Sterling?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.140
<v Jack Marlowe>Lucky guess.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.860
<v Knuckles Malone>Look, Marlow. The boss said to get the paper outta that hat before anybody gets

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.521
<v Knuckles Malone>to locker forty-seven!

00:01:17.599 --> 00:01:18.980
<v Knuckles Malone>Aw, nuts.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.580
<v Jack Marlowe>Thanks, Knuckles.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.620
<v Knuckles Malone>Hey! You didn't hear that from me!

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:24.820
<v Jack Marlowe>Hear what?

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.680
<v Knuckles Malone>Exactly! You're a real gentleman, detective.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.620
<v Jack Marlowe>I'll put another sandwich on my tab.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.440
<v Knuckles Malone>Make it pastrami. And extra pickles. Say, you ever need somebody roughed up, I

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.320
<v Knuckles Malone>got Tuesdays free.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.240
<v Jack Marlowe>I'll keep that in mind.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.620
<v Jack Marlowe>I left Knuckles to his second victim of the evening and found a telephone.

00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:48.500
<v Jack Marlowe>Betty, check the hat lining. Knuckles says there's a paper connected to Victor

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.324
<v Jack Marlowe>Sterling and locker forty-seven.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:56.080
<v Betty>Beat ya to it, boss! Found the paper and a little key inside the clasp.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.160
<v Betty>I'm lookin' up Sterling now.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.320
<v Jack Marlowe>Remind me why I get paid more than you.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.860
<v Betty>Because I ain't negotiated my raise yet!

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:11.100
<v Jack Marlowe>I headed back to the office. Sterling had a secret, Betty had the key, and Knuckles

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.220
<v Jack Marlowe>had indigestion. So far, everybody was getting what they deserved.

